course: dictionary
lesson: 4606
title: Saying hi
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Hi» is a short, friendly word. It means hello, and you say it when you meet someone. In «though they still say hi in the corridor», the children are greeting each other as they pass, so hi is a greeting.
explain: Hi is informal. Use it with friends and family. With a grown-up you do not know well, a more polite greeting such as «good morning» is better. Choosing the right greeting for the person you are talking to is part of reading the context too.
explain: Look at the words around hi. In «say hi to» someone, the phrase means give them a friendly greeting from you. Phrases like «hi there» and «hi everyone» are used in the same friendly way.
fact: «Hi» means hello. It is a greeting.
fact: «Say hi to» someone means give them a friendly greeting from you.
fact: Hi is informal: use it with friends and family.
fact: «Hi-vis» is a different word: it is short for high visibility, so hi-vis vests make workers easy to see.
fact: «Hi there» and «hi everyone» are common phrases that use hi in a friendly way.
exercise: In «they still say hi in the corridor», what are the children doing? | Asking for help | *Greeting each other | Counting the steps | Leaving the school
exercise: Which greeting is more polite for a grown-up you do not know well? | Hiya, you | Hi everyone | *Good morning | Hi, mate
exercise: In «hi-vis vests make workers easy to see», what does hi-vis mean? | *High visibility | High tide | Hello to everyone | Very quick
test: What does «say hi to» someone mean? | Say goodbye to them | Tell them a secret | Shout their name loudly | *Give them a friendly greeting from you
test: Which word is informal, the kind you use with friends? | *Hi | Pleased to meet you | Greetings, sir | Good afternoon
exam: Which sentence uses hi as a greeting? | Hi is a number, add it up | Please hi the door | *Hi, Ali, do you want to play? | Turn hi the page over
